// PARAM: --analysis sign
// A conversion that cannot possibly wrap still tops under Sign, and this is
// the sharpest form of the missing invariant because no wraparound is even
// reachable: uint8's range is a subset of int32's, so uint8-to-int32 is the
// identity on every value a uint8 can hold.
//
// Sign still has to give up. Answering NonNegative would claim
// ik_norm int32 v >= 0 for every v in gamma of NonNegative, and that gamma is
// unbounded, so v = 2^31 refutes it. The premise that would rescue it -- that
// z holds a uint8 -- is exactly what no abstract cell records, and teval reads
// a variable without normalizing, so it does not hold of every store the
// semantics admits either.
//
// The interval domain answers [0,255] on the same program, because its
// concretization is bounded and its conversion can check. That contrast is
// the argument for the kind-tagged cell in one line.
//
// 22-integer-kinds/precision/07-unsigned_conversion_is_nonnegative.vimp is the
// case Sign does get: a conversion *to* an unsigned kind, where ik_norm lands
// in [0, max] whatever the source value was, so no bound on the source is
// needed.
void main() {
  uint8 z;
  int32 q;
  z := __voblint_nondet_int();
  q := z;
  __voblint_check(!(q < 0)) // UNKNOWN
}
